[{"id":"/sicpjs/3.1.1","tag":"TITLE","body":"3.1.1  \n    Local State Variables"},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p1","child":[{"body":"\n    To illustrate what we mean by having a computational object with\n    \n    time-varying state, let us model the situation of withdrawing money\n    from a\n    \n    bank account.  We will do this using a\n    function","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":", which takes as argument an\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"amount"},{"body":" to be withdrawn.\n    If there is enough money in the account to accommodate the withdrawal,\n    then ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":" should return the balance\n    remaining after the withdrawal.  Otherwise,\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":" should return the message\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"EM","child":[{"body":"Insufficient funds.","tag":"#text"}]},{"body":" For example, if we begin with $100\n    in the account, we should obtain the following sequence of responses\n    using\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":":\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":1,"eval":true,"prependLength":12,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYDYFMAuIARgIbYkB2AxriALwioAMTA3FgGYCu1+AlgHsKIAO598ACwAmAJxIiAFCQC2AnvgCUIAN4YQ+kHw4gFpctVoA+BirUVNOvQednKNesTJvaAWhC31dmdnGQIuGWFXCyCDAF8QXGwAZ1pdYINQ-HDhACIICiSuDg4+Kj5cexBuCikknJj9WIwmjDFJWXkFACYAVg1WIA","body":"withdraw(25); ","output":"75"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":2,"eval":true,"prependLength":14,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYDYFMAuIARgIbYkB2AxriALwioAMTA3FgGYCu1+AlgHsKIAO598ACwAmAJxIiAFCQC2AnvgCUIAN4YQ+kHw4gFpctVoA+BirUVNOvQednKNesTJvaAWhC31dmdnGQIuGWFXCyCDAF8QXGwAZ1pdYINQ-HDhACIICiSuDg4+Kj5cexBuCikknJj9WIwmjDFJWXkFACYAVg12VvFpOUVe-qA","body":"withdraw(25); ","output":"50"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":3,"eval":true,"prependLength":16,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYDYFMAuIARgIbYkB2AxriALwioAMTA3FgGYCu1+AlgHsKIAO598ACwAmAJxIiAFCQC2AnvgCUIAN4YQ+kHw4gFpctVoA+BirUVNOvQednKNesTJvaAWhC31dmdnGQIuGWFXCyCDAF8QXGwAZ1pdYINQ-HDhACIICiSuDg4+Kj5cexBuCikknJj9WIwmjDFJWXkFACYAVg12VvFpOUVe-qw24c6ANiZ+oA","body":"withdraw(60); ","output":"\"Insufficient funds\""},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":4,"eval":true,"prependLength":18,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYDYFMAuIARgIbYkB2AxriALwioAMTA3FgGYCu1+AlgHsKIAO598ACwAmAJxIiAFCQC2AnvgCUIAN4YQ+kHw4gFpctVoA+BirUVNOvQednKNesTJvaAWhC31dmdnGQIuGWFXCyCDAF8QXGwAZ1pdYINQ-HDhACIICiSuDg4+Kj5cexBuCikknJj9WIwmjDFJWXkFACYAVg12VvFpOUVe-qw24c6ANiZxwfaRhVQ+1iA","body":"withdraw(15); ","output":"35"},{"body":"\n    Observe that the expression\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw(25)"},{"body":",\n      \n    evaluated twice, yields different values.  This is a new kind of\n    behavior for a\n    function.\n    Until now, all our\n    Python functions\n    could be viewed as specifications for computing mathematical functions.\n    A call to a\n    function\n    computed the value of the function applied to the given arguments,\n    and two calls to the same\n    function\n    with the same arguments always produced the same\n    result.","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"FOOTNOTE_REF","id":"#footnote-link-1","body":"1","href":"/sicpjs/3.1.1#footnote-1"}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p2","child":[{"body":"\n\tSo far, all our names have been ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"EM","child":[{"body":"immutable","tag":"#text"}]},{"body":". \n\tWhen a function was applied, the values that its parameters\n\treferred to never changed, and once a declaration was evaluated,\n\tthe declared name never changed its value.\n        To implement functions like\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":", we introduce\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"EM","child":[{"body":"variable declarations","tag":"#text"}]},{"body":", which use the keyword\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"let"},{"body":", in addition to constant\n\tdeclarations, which use the keyword\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"const"},{"body":".\n        We can declare a variable\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":"\n\tto indicate the balance of money\t\n\tin the account and define\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":" as a function that accesses\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":".\n      \n    The ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":"function\n    checks to see if ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" is at least as large\n    as the requested ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"amount"},{"body":".  If so,\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":" decrements\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" by ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"amount"},{"body":"\n    and returns the new value of ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":". Otherwise,\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":" returns the ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"EM","child":[{"body":"Insufficient funds","tag":"#text"}]},{"body":"\n    message. Here are the\n    declarations\n    of ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" and\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":":\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":5,"eval":true,"prependLength":0,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYDYFMAuIARgIbYkB2AxriALwioAMTA3FgGYCu1+AlgHsKIAO598ACwAmAJxIiAFCQC2AnvgCUIAN4YQ+kHw4gFpctVoA+BirUVNOvQednKNesTJvaAWhC31dmdnGQIuGWFXCyCDAF8QXGwAZ1pdYINQ-HDhACIICiSuDg4+Kj5cexBuCikknJj9WIwmjDFJWXkFACYAVg1WIA","body":"let balance = 100;\n\nfunction withdraw(amount) {\n    if (balance >= amount) {\n        balance = balance - amount;\n        return balance;\n    } else {\n        return \"Insufficient funds\";\n    }\n} "},{"body":"\n    Decrementing ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" is accomplished by the \n    expression statement","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":6,"eval":false,"body":"balance = balance - amount;"},{"body":"\n\tThe syntax of\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"EM","child":[{"body":"assignment","tag":"#text"}]},{"body":" expressions is\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":true,"eval":false,"body":"\n$name$ = $new$-$value$\n      "},{"body":"\n    Here\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"META","body":"name"},{"body":"\n\thas been declared with\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"let"},{"body":" or\n\tas a\n\t\n\tfunction parameter\n      \n    and\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"META","body":"new-value"},{"body":"\n    is any expression.  \n    The assignment \n    changes\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"META","body":"name"},{"body":"\n    so that its value is the\n    result obtained by evaluating\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"META","body":"new-value"},{"body":".\n      \n    In the case at hand, we are changing ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" so\n    that its new value will be the result of subtracting\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"amount"},{"body":" from the previous value of\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":".","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"FOOTNOTE_REF","id":"#footnote-link-2","body":"2","href":"/sicpjs/3.1.1#footnote-2"}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p3","child":[{"body":"\n\tThe function ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":" also uses a\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"EM","child":[{"body":"sequence of statements","tag":"#text"}]},{"body":" to cause two statements to be evaluated\n\tin the case where the ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"if"},{"body":" test is\n\ttrue: first decrementing  ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":"\n\tand then returning the value of\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":".  \n\tIn general, executing a sequence\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":true,"eval":false,"body":"\n$stmt$$_{1}$ $stmt$$_{2} \\ldots$$stmt$$_{n}$\n          "},{"body":"\n        causes the statements ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"META","body":"stmt"},{"body":"$_{1}$","tag":"LATEX"},{"body":"\n\tthrough\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"META","body":"stmt"},{"body":"$_{n}$","tag":"LATEX"},{"body":" to be evaluated in\n\tsequence.","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"FOOTNOTE_REF","id":"#footnote-link-3","body":"3","href":"/sicpjs/3.1.1#footnote-3"}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p4","child":[{"body":"\n    Although ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":" works as desired, the\n    variable ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" presents a problem.  As\n    specified above, ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" is a name defined\n    in the\n    program environment and is freely accessible to be examined or\n      modified by any\n      function.\n      It would be much better if we could somehow make\n      ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" internal to\n      ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":", so that\n      ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":" would be the only\n      function\n      that could access ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" directly and\n      any other\n      function\n      could access ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" only indirectly\n      (through calls to ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":").  This would\n      more accurately model the notion that\n      ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" is a local state variable used by\n      ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":" to keep track of the state of the\n      account.\n  ","tag":"#text"}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p5","child":[{"body":"\n    We can make ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" internal to\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":" by rewriting the definition as\n    follows:\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":7,"eval":true,"prependLength":0,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYGYFcB2AxgC4CWA9viALYCGA1gKYD6A7qcQBYAmATra2YAjWgBtaRFqgAM0gBQBKEAG8MIdSFGNiIEeMkgAvCBnSA3Go29tuXlVrVyBHYYB8Kyxq-eQpbCDk9CUJGEFdjByd8YiVVH3ifIINjJJCQAFoQSOcLBLz1a2JbKlTGXPyvAF8QRlEAZ1C4ivjC4pAAIgh8OtxsbFJCUkZokDx8bjr28uaQSs8Eyos5wko6nXxGQXYuPgEjGgYWbZ5+QVLmU0ULDA2tjhOBOQA2aQULW7Z73dZn17MgA","body":"function make_withdraw_balance_100() {\n    let balance = 100;\n    return amount => {\n               if (balance >= amount) {\n                   balance = balance - amount;\n                   return balance;\n               } else {\n                   return \"Insufficient funds\";\n               }\n           };\n}\nconst new_withdraw = make_withdraw_balance_100(); "},{"body":"\n        What we have done here is use ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"let"},{"body":"\n\tto establish an environment with a local variable\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":", bound to the initial\n\tvalue 100. Within this local environment, we use a lambda\n\texpression","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"FOOTNOTE_REF","id":"#footnote-link-4","body":"4","href":"/sicpjs/3.1.1#footnote-4"},{"body":" to\n\tcreate a function that takes ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"amount"},{"body":"\n\tas an argument and behaves like our previous\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":" function.  This\n\tfunction—returned as the result of evaluating the body of the\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"make_withdraw_balance_100"},{"body":"\n\tfunction—behaves in precisely the same way as\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":", but its variable\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" is not accessible by any\n\tother function.","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"FOOTNOTE_REF","id":"#footnote-link-5","body":"5","href":"/sicpjs/3.1.1#footnote-5"}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p6","child":[{"body":"\n    Combining \n    \n        assignments with variable declarations\n      \n    is the general programming\n    technique we will use for constructing computational objects with\n    local state.  Unfortunately, using this technique raises a serious\n    problem: When we first introduced\n    functions,\n    we also introduced the substitution model of evaluation\n    (section ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"REF","body":"1.1.5","href":"/sicpjs/1.1.5"},{"body":") to provide an\n    interpretation of what\n    function\n    application means.  We said that applying a\n    function whose body is a return statement\n    should be interpreted as evaluating the\n    return expression of the function\n    with the\n    \n    parameters replaced by their values.\n    \n\tFor functions with more complex\n\tbodies, we need to evaluate the whole body with the\n\tparameters replaced by their values.\n      \n    The trouble is that,\n    as soon as we introduce assignment into our language, substitution is no\n    longer an adequate model of\n    function\n    application.  (We will see why this is so in\n    section ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"REF","body":"3.1.3","href":"/sicpjs/3.1.3"},{"body":".)  As a consequence, we\n    technically have at this point no way to understand why the\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"new_withdraw"},{"body":"function\n    behaves as claimed above.  In order to really understand a\n    function\n    such as\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"new_withdraw"},{"body":",\n      \n    we will need to develop a new model of\n    function\n    application.  In section ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"REF","body":"3.2","href":"/sicpjs/3.2"},{"body":" we will\n    introduce such a model, together with an explanation of \n    assignments and variable declarations.\n    First, however, we examine some variations on the theme established by\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"new_withdraw"},{"body":".\n      ","tag":"#text"}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p7","child":[{"body":"\n\tParameters of functions as well as names declared with\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"let"},{"body":" are\n\t\n\tvariables.\n      \n    The following\n    \n\tfunction, ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"make_withdraw"},{"body":",\n      \n    creates \"","tag":"#text"},{"body":"withdrawal processors.","tag":"#text"},{"body":"\"\n    The  parameter\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" in\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"make_withdraw"},{"body":"\n    specifies the initial amount of money in the\n    account.","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"FOOTNOTE_REF","id":"#footnote-link-6","body":"6","href":"/sicpjs/3.1.1#footnote-6"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":8,"eval":true,"prependLength":0,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYGYFcB2AxgC4CWA9viALYCGA1gKYD6A7qcQBYAmATrawAUAI1oAbWkUYBKEAG8MIJSF6NiuXlVrVyBYiAC8APnmLl5i0tLYQI8ZMKMQRgyG278xWQsu-LoiSlDEACHJwBaNx09AG4zPwTVdU0Q+yk4hMsAXxBGMQBnJx9MvySNKgAiCHx83GxsUkJSRk8QPHxufIqMkuUs+L8suP6MQkp8-QB1VGC6JjYOHn4hVAAGVek4sZqpgCZZhhZ2Lj4BQTWNmKA","body":"function make_withdraw(balance) {\n    return amount => {\n               if (balance >= amount) {\n                   balance = balance - amount;\n                   return balance;\n               } else {\n                   return \"Insufficient funds\";\n               }\n           };\n} "},{"body":"\n\tThe function ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"make_withdraw"},{"body":"\n    can be used as follows to create two objects ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"W1"},{"body":"\n    and ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"W2"},{"body":":\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":9,"eval":true,"prependLength":12,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYGYFcB2AxgC4CWA9viALYCGA1gKYD6A7qcQBYAmATrawAUAI1oAbWkUYBKEAG8MIJSF6NiuXlVrVyBYiAC8APnmLl5i0tLYQI8ZMKMQRgyG278xWQsu-LoiSlDEACHJwBaNx09AG4zPwTVdU0Q+yk4hMsAXxBGMQBnJx9MvySNKgAiCHx83GxsUkJSRk8QPHxufIqMkuUs+L8suP6MQkp8-QB1VGC6JjYOHn4hVAAGVek4sZqpgCZZhhZ2Lj4BQTWNmKA","body":"const W1 = make_withdraw(100);\nconst W2 = make_withdraw(100); "},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":10,"eval":true,"prependLength":15,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYGYFcB2AxgC4CWA9viALYCGA1gKYD6A7qcQBYAmATrawAUAI1oAbWkUYBKEAG8MIJSF6NiuXlVrVyBYiAC8APnmLl5i0tLYQI8ZMKMQRgyG278xWQsu-LoiSlDEACHJwBaNx09AG4zPwTVdU0Q+yk4hMsAXxBGMQBnJx9MvySNKgAiCHx83GxsUkJSRk8QPHxufIqMkuUs+L8suP6MQkp8-QB1VGC6JjYOHn4hVAAGVek4sZqpgCZZhhZ2Lj4BQTWNuIxpwQBWS6A","body":"W1(50); ","output":"50"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":11,"eval":true,"prependLength":17,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYGYFcB2AxgC4CWA9viALYCGA1gKYD6A7qcQBYAmATrawAUAI1oAbWkUYBKEAG8MIJSF6NiuXlVrVyBYiAC8APnmLl5i0tLYQI8ZMKMQRgyG278xWQsu-LoiSlDEACHJwBaNx09AG4zPwTVdU0Q+yk4hMsAXxBGMQBnJx9MvySNKgAiCHx83GxsUkJSRk8QPHxufIqMkuUs+L8suP6MQkp8-QB1VGC6JjYOHn4hVAAGVek4sZqpgCZZhhZ2Lj4BQTWNuIxpwQBWS6xJ3cEAdkugA","body":"W2(70); ","output":"30"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":12,"eval":true,"prependLength":19,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYGYFcB2AxgC4CWA9viALYCGA1gKYD6A7qcQBYAmATrawAUAI1oAbWkUYBKEAG8MIJSF6NiuXlVrVyBYiAC8APnmLl5i0tLYQI8ZMKMQRgyG278xWQsu-LoiSlDEACHJwBaNx09AG4zPwTVdU0Q+yk4hMsAXxBGMQBnJx9MvySNKgAiCHx83GxsUkJSRk8QPHxufIqMkuUs+L8suP6MQkp8-QB1VGC6JjYOHn4hVAAGVek4sZqpgCZZhhZ2Lj4BQTWNuIxpwQBWS6xJ3cEAdgfr54AWS6A","body":"W2(40); ","output":"\"Insufficient funds\""},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":13,"eval":true,"prependLength":21,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYGYFcB2AxgC4CWA9viALYCGA1gKYD6A7qcQBYAmATrawAUAI1oAbWkUYBKEAG8MIJSF6NiuXlVrVyBYiAC8APnmLl5i0tLYQI8ZMKMQRgyG278xWQsu-LoiSlDEACHJwBaNx09AG4zPwTVdU0Q+yk4hMsAXxBGMQBnJx9MvySNKgAiCHx83GxsUkJSRk8QPHxufIqMkuUs+L8suP6MQkp8-QB1VGC6JjYOHn4hVAAGVek4sZqpgCZZhhZ2Lj4BQTWNuIxpwQBWS6xJ3cEAdgfr54AWd5vvzaA","body":"W1(40); ","output":"10"},{"body":"\n    Observe that ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"W1"},{"body":" and \n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"W2"},{"body":" are completely independent objects, each\n    with its own local state variable ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":".\n    Withdrawals from one do not affect the other.\n  ","tag":"#text"}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p8","child":[{"body":"\n    We can also create objects that handle\n    \n    deposits as well as\n    withdrawals, and thus we can represent simple bank accounts.  Here is\n    a\n    function\n    that returns a \"","tag":"#text"},{"body":"bank-account object","tag":"#text"},{"body":"\" with a specified initial\n    balance:\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":14,"eval":true,"prependLength":0,"program":"chap=3&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniAzAOgIxoFAYGYFcB2AxgC4CWA9viALYCGA1gKYD6thh5BxAFAEa0AbWkUYBKEAG8MIGSDxEylEAHdSxABYATAE61l3WtU75i4qbIshS2EH0HDCjEAD4AvCEPHTk6Zb-8hERB3AIcnAFoPIy4Abl8-C21GYlxtKlCROISQAF8QRgEAZydzbNkklLSQACIIfELcbGxSQlJGEzkCTULqrISc+NzB+RIKKk1GAAdyQrUDaJMzQYsMx2CQVacAaiivPr8K1PT7TMGBixHFcdJCydpiQnVuaiXsw6rqYNd3atUNHT01WWZRAAH4VGotLplMCygAuGhfH4TaazYhAkGWcEomZqWHZBGMbTacjaZ4AGhqBHo+HIyioSQAjrhGIViCBwpE6ExWOwvNVRPsholkkcQJobncHuo4gMMBx6uy2IR1tyWMqvNxUAAGbWCrDK7i-SEA5QC7gAVj1MSAA","body":"function make_account(balance) {\n    function withdraw(amount) {\n        if (balance >= amount) {\n            balance = balance - amount;\n            return balance;\n        } else {\n            return \"Insufficient funds\";\n        }\n    }\n    function deposit(amount) {\n        balance = balance + amount;\n        return balance;\n    }\n    function dispatch(m) {\n        return m === \"withdraw\"\n               ? withdraw\n               : m === \"deposit\"\n               ? deposit\n               : error(m, \"unknown request -- make_account\");\n    }\n    return dispatch;\n} "},{"body":"\n    Each call to ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"make_account"},{"body":" sets up an\n    environment with a local state variable ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":".\n    Within this environment, ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"make_account"},{"body":" defines\n    functions","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"deposit"},{"body":" and\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"withdraw"},{"body":" that access\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"balance"},{"body":" and an additional\n    function","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"dispatch"},{"body":"\n    that takes a \"","tag":"#text"},{"body":"message","tag":"#text"},{"body":"\" as input and returns one of the two local\n    functions.\n    The ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"dispatch"},{"body":"function\n    itself is returned as the value that represents the bank-account object.\n    This is precisely the \n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"EM","child":[{"body":"message-passing","tag":"#text"}]},{"body":" style of programming that we saw in\n    section ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"REF","body":"2.4.3","href":"/sicpjs/2.4.3"},{"body":", although here we are using\n    it in conjunction with the ability to modify local variables.\n  ","tag":"#text"}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p9","child":[{"body":"\n\tThe function\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"make_account"},{"body":"\n    can be used as follows:\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":15,"eval":true,"prependLength":24,"progra